    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": " \n                          VETO MESSAGE - No. 98\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 1419, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to amend the executive law, in relation to requiring agen-\n      cies to provide unsuccessful bidders that are  certified  minority\n      and  women-owned  business  enterprises  with  a written statement\n      articulating the reasons for such rejection\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would require that Minority and Women-owned Business  Enter-\nprises (MWBEs) who are rejected from a bid be given a mandatory briefing\non the reasons for the denial.\n \n  I  am a strong supporter of the MWBE program and recognize the need to\nexpand opportunities for the MWBEs in New  York.  However,  this  legis-\nlation  is  unnecessary and duplicative because, under the existing law,\nunsuccessful bidders are already allowed  to  request  a  debriefing  to\nunderstand the reasons for deficiencies that result in a denial.\n \n  Therefore, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
    "vetoNumber": 98,
